  "intro": {
    "en": "In week 1 we only looked at the male Blackbird and the male House Sparrow. That was on purpose: the females look completely different. A brown \"blackbird\" is not a different bird; it's the female of the same species. Today we meet the other half.\n\nFor each bird in this lesson there's a bird you've met before. First look for the shape you already know. Then check the colours: females are usually brown, grey or streaky, which helps them hide on the nest.\n\nYoung birds wear a plumage of their own for a while. We take one example, the young Mute Swan. At the end there's a quiz of ten questions, with birds from the last two weeks mixed in."
  },
